---
epr-meta-version: 1
id: claude-handoffs-holding-pen
purpose: >
  A deprecated holding pen for session handoffs written before the decompose discipline replaced
  them. Handoff documents are not an artifact class here, so no new document is born in this
  directory. The files still present wait to be decomposed and removed
  (genesis/data/timeline/backlog/handoff-sprawl-decompose-2026-06-23.md).
rules:
  - id: handoff-routes-to-sprints
    class: dispatch
    when: { write: "*.md", new: true }
    route-to: { dest: genesis/docs/superpowers/sprints/ }
    parameters:
      dispatch-agent: librarian
      dispatch-prompt: >
        Review the proposed new markdown document for context pollution. Return exactly one
        recommendation: ROUTE with a canonical destination (a sprint result under
        genesis/docs/superpowers/sprints/, a backlog entry, a memory file, or a shift objective),
        MERGE into an existing artifact, or DROP as session-scoped, with the shortest supporting
        reason. Do not create, move, or rewrite files; report to the editing agent and let
        development continue.
    why: >
      The handoff pattern was retired in df250665f (2026-06-11), and this directory became a
      holding pen for undecomposed handoffs on 2026-06-23 (archive/README.md). About a dozen more
      were born here after that. A concluded session's durable carrier is its sprint result in
      genesis/docs/superpowers/sprints/. Decompose the rest: open work to
      genesis/data/timeline/backlog/, a lesson to a memory file or to
      genesis/docs/content/elohim-protocol/history/, and the narration to git history. A shift
      objective belongs in .claude/shifts/<shift-id>.objective.json.
    retire-when: >
      when the undecomposed handoffs here have been harvested and removed and the directory itself
      is deleted, leaving nothing to route
---
# .claude/handoffs — deprecated holding pen

`archive/README.md` records the rule: finish a shift by decomposing, not by writing a handoff.
This manifest enforces the birth side of that rule. It re-declares the repo-root rule id
`handoff-routes-to-sprints` (nearest wins) and widens the match from `handoff*.md` to every
markdown birth here. That catches `OBJECTIVE-*.md`, dated `*-handoff.md` and `*-RESULT.md` files
too, and a `HANDOFF-*.md` born here gets one review, not two.

Editing an existing file here is never routed; only a new file is.
